      "math_academy_id": "q-275231",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$  \n\n{{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}},\n\n{{field-3}}\n\n$⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (-1)+8\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot (-2)}{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{14}⟨-1,3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨-1,3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,6,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
